# Stop the service when a question session ends

A question session **ends** when the user has no more questions (or says they are done) after the implementation summary / Q&A (`10-end-of-session-questions.mdc`). Do not leave Docker from that question running.

## Required script

Every `questions/<slug>/` folder (and every **implemented** concept demo under `core-concepts/` or `key-technologies/`) must have `scripts/stop.sh` that:

- `cd`s to the question directory
- runs `docker compose down` (no `-v`; keep named volumes unless the user asks to wipe data)
- is idempotent (succeeds if nothing is running)
- does **not** print "not implemented"

Create it in the same pass if it is missing (copy from `_templates/question/scripts/stop.sh` or `_templates/concept/scripts/stop.sh`).

## When to run it

1. Record the last Q&A (or that they had none).
2. Run that folder’s `scripts/stop.sh` in that same turn.
3. Tell the user the stack is down and how to start it again (`./scripts/setup.sh`).

Do not wait for them to ask to stop. Do not skip this because the session already committed. Do not `docker compose down -v` unless they want data gone.

```bash
# ✅ GOOD — session closed
./scripts/stop.sh

# ❌ BAD — leave compose up after "we're done"
# ❌ BAD — only tell them to run `docker compose down` by hand
```
